434	/**
435	 * Insert the case entity, tolerating a collision on
436	 * `entities_slug_parent_unique (organization_id, COALESCE(parent_id, 0), slug)`.
437	 *
438	 * The slug cannot be treated as the identity. `slugifyCaseKey` is lossy — a run
439	 * promoted under `angle-a`, `angle_a` and `Angle A` produces one slug for three
440	 * different questions — and the index is NOT partial on `deleted_at`, so a
441	 * retired case keeps holding its slug forever. Adopting whichever row owns the
442	 * slug would fold distinct cases together and then replay them under the wrong
443	 * `case_key`, which is the wrong idempotency key. So adopt only the row that is
444	 * genuinely this (run, key) — the real recovery case, a promote that died
445	 * between the insert and its identity claim — and otherwise take a suffixed
446	 * slug. The `entity_identities` claim is the identity; the slug is cosmetic.
